fullCyclicPolytope -- Cyclic polytope.
**************************************

  * Usage: 
        fullCyclicPolytope(d,R)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, positive
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, an *note embedded complex: Complex,, 

Description
===========

Returns the full cyclic polytope of dimension d with vertices the variables of
R. A coker grading is added to R via the vertices of the moment curve (if R
already has a coker grading then a warning is displayed) and translated such
that 0 lies in the interior of C.



+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x_0..x_5]                                                       |
|                                                                          |
|o1 = R                                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C=fullCyclicPolytope(3,R)                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o2 = 3: x x x x x x                                                       |
|         0 1 2 3 4 5                                                      |
|                                                                          |
|o2 : complex of dim 3 embedded in dim 3 (printing facets)                 |
|     equidimensional, non-simplicial, F-vector {1, 6, 12, 8, 1}, Euler = 0|
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note boundaryCyclicPolytope: boundaryCyclicPolytope, -- The boundary
    complex of a cyclic polytope.

