possibleDenominators -- Possible denominators of deformations.
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        possibleDenominators(I)
        possibleDenominators(I,v)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, monomial, reduced.
      * v, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of variables of *note ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ring, I.
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Computes a list L of possible denominators of Laurent monomials representing
*note FirstOrderDeformation: FirstOrderDeformation,s of I. The list L is
stratified into lists with ascending degree of the denominators. Each
denominator is represented as a list of variables.

If the second argument v is given, one obtains only denominators contained (as
a list) in v.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x_0..x_4];                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal(x_0*x_1,x_1*x_2,x_2*x_3,x_3*x_4,x_4*x_0);                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : possibleDenominators(I)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{{x }, {x }, {x }, {x }, {x }}, {{x , x }, {x , x }, {x , x }, {x ,    |
|         0     1     2     3     4       0   1     1   2     2   3     0     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x }, {x , x }}}                                                         |
|      4     3   4                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : possibleDenominators(I,{x_0,x_1,x_2});                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note deformationsFace: deformationsFace, -- Compute the deformations
    associated to a face.
  * *note deform: deform, -- Compute the deformations associated to a
    Stanley-Reisner complex.

